IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ea-core`

-- Employment Act 1968 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation
-- "version in force from 5/12/2025" -- LAYER 1, PART 14, SECTIONS 107A TO 114 (daily rates, wrongful detention,
-- general offences and penalties, bodies corporate, compounding).  Part ea2.
-- Source text: inputs/EmA1968.txt (a converter rendering, not the official text).
--
-- Notes for the reader.
--   * Seam S6: the daily rates of ss 107A come from the Third Schedule; they arrive as `the answer of sch 3 gross rate of pay per day`
--     and `the answer of sch 3 basic rate of pay per day`.
--   * Seam S15 is ANSWERED here: `s 112 first conviction` and `s 112 subsequent conviction`, each a MAYBE `Penalty on conviction`.
--   * Section 113A(7) (regulations) is a power and has no function here.
--   * A plain BOOLEAN or NUMBER answer is a date or count comparison and carries no legal "no".

§ `Part 14 -- the daily rates of pay of an employee on a monthly rate or piece rates (s 107A)`

-- s 107A(1): "The gross rate of pay per day of an employee employed on a monthly rate or on piece rates is to be calculated in
-- accordance with the second column of the Third Schedule."
-- src:4425 | 107A.—(1) The gross rate of pay per day of an employee employed
-- src:4426 | on a monthly rate or on piece rates is to be calculated in accordance
-- src:4427 | with the second column of the Third Schedule.
@ref s 107A(1) (src:4425-4427)
GIVEN `the employee is employed on a monthly rate or on piece rates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of sch 3 gross rate of pay per day` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 107A(1) the gross rate of pay per day` MEANS
    IF `the employee is employed on a monthly rate or on piece rates`
    THEN `the answer of sch 3 gross rate of pay per day`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of an employee employed on a monthly rate or on piece rates
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 107A(2): "The basic rate of pay per day of an employee employed on a monthly rate or on piece rates is to be calculated in
-- accordance with the third column of the Third Schedule."
-- src:4429 | (2) The basic rate of pay per day of an employee employed on a
-- src:4430 | monthly rate or on piece rates is to be calculated in accordance with
-- src:4431 | the third column of the Third Schedule.
@ref s 107A(2) (src:4429-4431)
GIVEN `the employee is employed on a monthly rate or on piece rates` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the answer of sch 3 basic rate of pay per day` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 107A(2) the basic rate of pay per day` MEANS
    IF `the employee is employed on a monthly rate or on piece rates`
    THEN `the answer of sch 3 basic rate of pay per day`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of an employee employed on a monthly rate or on piece rates
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Part 14 -- wrongful detention, debts of others, obstruction (ss 108 to 111)`

-- s 108: "Any employer who without reasonable excuse, the proof of which is to lie on the employer, refuses to allow an employee
-- whose contract of service has been determined in any of the ways provided in this Act to leave the employer's service shall be
-- guilty of an offence".  The proof of reasonable excuse lies on the employer: an excuse not proved is no excuse.
-- src:4435 | 108. Any employer who without reasonable excuse, the proof of
-- src:4436 | which is to lie on the employer, refuses to allow an employee whose
-- src:4437 | contract of service has been determined in any of the ways provided
-- src:4438 | in this Act to leave the employer’s service shall be guilty of an
-- src:4439 | offence and shall be liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding
-- src:4440 | $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to
-- src:4441 | both, and the whole or any portion of any fine recoverable under this
-- src:4442 | section may be adjudged by the court to be paid to the employee.
@ref s 108 (src:4435-4442)
GIVEN `the employer refused to allow the employee, whose contract of service has been determined in a way provided in the Act, to leave the employer's service` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the employer has proved a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 108 the employer is guilty of an offence` MEANS
    IF `the employer refused to allow the employee, whose contract of service has been determined in a way provided in the Act, to leave the employer's service` AND (NOT `the employer has proved a reasonable excuse`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the offence is refusing, without a reasonable excuse proved by the employer, to allow an employee whose contract has been determined to leave the employer's service
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 108 (src:4435-4442)
GIVETH A `Penalty on conviction`
`s 108 the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    `Penalty on conviction` WITH
        `least fine in dollars` IS 0
        `greatest fine in dollars` IS JUST 5000
        `longest imprisonment in months` IS JUST 6

-- s 108: "the whole or any portion of any fine recoverable under this section may be adjudged by the court to be paid to the employee."
@ref s 108 (src:4435-4442)
GIVEN `the employer is convicted of an offence under section 108 and a fine is recoverable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 108 the court may adjudge the whole or any portion of the fine to be paid to the employee` MEANS
    IF `the employer is convicted of an offence under section 108 and a fine is recoverable`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is over a fine recoverable under section 108
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 109: "An employee is not bound, by virtue of any contract of service under this Act, to answer for the debt, default or
