    IF `the liability is claimed by virtue of a contract of service under this Act`
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An employee is not bound, by virtue of any contract of service under this Act, to answer for the debt"
    THEN JUST FALSE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section speaks of a liability claimed by virtue of a contract of service under this Act
    ELSE NOTHING

