§ `Part 14 -- the default penalty, abetment, inducing emigration (ss 112 to 113)`

-- s 112: "Any person who is guilty of any breach or any offence under this Act for which no penalty is otherwise provided shall be
-- liable on conviction to a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 6 months or to both, and for a
-- subsequent offence under the same section to a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12
-- months or to both."  Seam S15: the two penalties, for the caller to choose between.
-- src:4470 | 112. Any person who is guilty of any breach or any offence under
-- src:4471 | this Act for which no penalty is otherwise provided shall be liable on
-- src:4472 | conviction to a fine not exceeding $5,000 or to imprisonment for a
-- src:4473 | term not exceeding 6 months or to both, and for a subsequent offence
-- src:4474 | under the same section to a fine not exceeding $10,000 or to
-- src:4475 | imprisonment for a term not exceeding 12 months or to both.
@ref s 112 (src:4470-4475)
GIVETH A MAYBE (`Penalty on conviction`)
`s 112 first conviction` MEANS
    JUST (`Penalty on conviction` WITH
        `least fine in dollars` IS 0
        `greatest fine in dollars` IS JUST 5000
        `longest imprisonment in months` IS JUST 6)

@ref s 112 (src:4470-4475)
GIVETH A MAYBE (`Penalty on conviction`)
`s 112 subsequent conviction` MEANS
    JUST (`Penalty on conviction` WITH
        `least fine in dollars` IS 0
        `greatest fine in dollars` IS JUST 10000
        `longest imprisonment in months` IS JUST 12)

@ref s 112 (src:4470-4475)
GIVEN `no penalty is otherwise provided for the breach or offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a subsequent offence under the same section` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (`Penalty on conviction`)
`s 112 the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    IF `no penalty is otherwise provided for the breach or offence`
    THEN
        IF `it is a subsequent offence under the same section`
        THEN `s 112 subsequent conviction`
        ELSE `s 112 first conviction`
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section is for a breach or offence "for which no penalty is otherwise provided"
    ELSE NOTHING

-- s 112A: "Any person who abets the commission of an offence under this Act shall be guilty of the offence and shall be liable on
-- conviction to be punished with the punishment provided for that offence."
-- src:4479 | 112A. Any person who abets the commission of an offence under
-- src:4480 | this Act shall be guilty of the offence and shall be liable on conviction
-- src:4481 | to be punished with the punishment provided for that offence.
@ref s 112A (src:4479-4481)
GIVEN `the person abets the commission of an offence under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 112A the person is guilty of the offence abetted` MEANS
    IF `the person abets the commission of an offence under the Act`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the section is of "Any person who abets the commission of an offence under this Act"
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 112A (src:4479-4481)
GIVEN `the penalty provided for the offence abetted` IS A `Penalty on conviction`
GIVETH A `Penalty on conviction`
`s 112A the punishment of the person who abets` MEANS
    `the penalty provided for the offence abetted`

