    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the offence is inducing or attempting to induce a person, by force, intoxication or ill-treatment, intimidation, fraud or false representations, to enter into a contract of service to work beyond the limits of Singapore
    ELSE NOTHING

@ref s 113 (src:4487-4494)
GIVETH A `Penalty on conviction`
`s 113 the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    `Penalty on conviction` WITH
        `least fine in dollars` IS 0
        `greatest fine in dollars` IS JUST 5000
        `longest imprisonment in months` IS JUST 24

§ `Part 14 -- offences by bodies corporate and other bodies, and compounding (ss 113A and 114)`

-- s 113A(1): "Where an offence under this Act committed by a body corporate is proved (a) to have been committed with the consent
-- or connivance of an officer of the body corporate; or (b) to be attributable to any neglect on the officer's part, the officer as
-- well as the body corporate shall be guilty of the offence".
-- src:4496 | 113A.—(1) Where an offence under this Act committed by a body
-- src:4497 | corporate is proved —
-- src:4499 | (a) to have been committed with the consent or connivance of
-- src:4500 | an officer of the body corporate; or
-- src:4502 | (b) to be attributable to any neglect on the officer’s part,
-- src:4504 | the officer as well as the body corporate shall be guilty of the offence
-- src:4505 | and shall be liable to be proceeded against and punished accordingly.
@ref s 113A(1) (src:4496-4505)
GIVEN `an offence under the Act committed by a body corporate is proved` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it was committed with the consent or connivance of the officer` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is attributable to neglect on the officer's part` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 113A(1) the officer of the body corporate is guilty of the offence as well` MEANS
    IF `an offence under the Act committed by a body corporate is proved` AND (`it was committed with the consent or connivance of the officer` OR `it is attributable to neglect on the officer's part`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where an offence under this Act committed by a body corporate is proved"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- s 113A(2): "Where the affairs of a body corporate are managed by its members, subsection (1) applies in relation to the acts and
-- defaults of a member in connection with his or her functions of management as if he or she were a director of the body corporate."
-- src:4512 | (2) Where the affairs of a body corporate are managed by its
-- src:4513 | members, subsection (1) applies in relation to the acts and defaults of
-- src:4514 | a member in connection with his or her functions of management as if
-- src:4515 | he or she were a director of the body corporate.
@ref s 113A(2) (src:4512-4515)
GIVEN `the affairs of the body corporate are managed by its members` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the acts and defaults are of a member in connection with his or her functions of management` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 113A(2) subsection (1) applies to the member as if he or she were a director` MEANS
    IF `the affairs of the body corporate are managed by its members` AND `the acts and defaults are of a member in connection with his or her functions of management`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the affairs of a body corporate are managed by its members"
    ELSE JUST FALSE

