-- s 113A(5): "where an offence under this Act has been committed by a body corporate, an unincorporated association (other than a
-- partnership) or a partnership, it is presumed, until the contrary is proved, that the offence is attributable to the neglect of an
-- officer or a member ... or a partner ... who (a) is primarily responsible for the act or omission which constitutes the offence;
-- and (b) has failed to exercise reasonable supervision or oversight as such officer, member or partner."
-- src:4548 | (5) For the purposes of this section, where an offence under this Act
-- src:4549 | has been committed by a body corporate, an unincorporated
-- src:4550 | association (other than a partnership) or a partnership, it is
-- src:4551 | presumed, until the contrary is proved, that the offence is
-- src:4552 | attributable to the neglect of an officer or a member of the body
-- src:4553 | corporate or unincorporated association or a partner of the
-- src:4554 | partnership (as the case may be) who —
-- src:4556 | (a) is primarily responsible for the act or omission which
-- src:4557 | constitutes the offence; and
-- src:4562 | (b) has failed to exercise reasonable supervision or oversight
-- src:4563 | as such officer, member or partner.
@ref s 113A(5) (src:4548-4563)
GIVEN `an offence under the Act has been committed by a body corporate, an unincorporated association other than a partnership, or a partnership` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is primarily responsible for the act or omission which constitutes the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has failed to exercise reasonable supervision or oversight as such officer, member or partner` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the contrary has been proved` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 113A(5) the offence is presumed to be attributable to the neglect of the person` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where an offence under this Act has been committed by a body corporate, an unincorporated association"
        IF NOT `an offence under the Act has been committed by a body corporate, an unincorporated association other than a partnership, or a partnership` THEN JUST FALSE
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "it is presumed, until the contrary is proved, that the offence is attributable to the neglect of"
        IF `an offence under the Act has been committed by a body corporate, an unincorporated association other than a partnership, or a partnership` AND `the contrary has been proved` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `an offence under the Act has been committed by a body corporate, an unincorporated association other than a partnership, or a partnership`
           AND `the person is primarily responsible for the act or omission which constitutes the offence`
           AND `the person has failed to exercise reasonable supervision or oversight as such officer, member or partner`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the presumption is of the neglect of the officer, member or partner who is primarily responsible for the act or omission and has failed to exercise reasonable supervision or oversight
        OTHERWISE NOTHING

