-- s 114: "The Commissioner may compound any such offence under this Act as may be prescribed as being an offence which may be
-- compounded by accepting from the person reasonably suspected of committing that offence a sum not exceeding $5,000."
-- src:4602 | 114. The Commissioner may compound any such offence under
-- src:4603 | this Act as may be prescribed as being an offence which may be
-- src:4604 | compounded by accepting from the person reasonably suspected of
-- src:4605 | committing that offence a sum not exceeding $5,000.
@ref s 114 (src:4602-4605)
GIVEN `the offence is one prescribed as an offence which may be compounded` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is reasonably suspected of committing the offence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sum offered in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 114 the Commissioner may compound the offence by accepting the sum` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a sum not exceeding $5,000"
        IF `the sum offered in dollars` GREATER THAN 5000 THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `the offence is one prescribed as an offence which may be compounded` AND `the person is reasonably suspected of committing the offence` THEN JUST TRUE
        -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the power is over an offence prescribed as one which may be compounded, from the person reasonably suspected of committing it
        OTHERWISE NOTHING
